   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 1,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Testing-only workflow for the sweep harness; hidden from the template browser. Based on dgx-monarch-ltx25-t2v, with only the changes needed for this test. One render cuts between shots and keeps the same people, room, light and voice across the cuts. There is no multishot node: the whole feature lives in the prompt, so the leg needs a template that carries one. The vendor's rules, which this prompt follows: one chronological paragraph rather than a shot list, each transition named in plain words, the new shot re-established after every cut, the same words for a recurring person, and the soundtrack described across the cuts. Two to four shots per render is the working range. Shape, schedule and sampler stay the base graph's."
   ],
   "title": "DGX Monarch | LTX 2.5 multishot text to video with sound"
  },
